title: April Conference of the <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span>
subtitle: The new leadership seeks a merger with leftist elements hostile to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communist Party**</span>...
view-if: stegerwald_skibidi_time == time and (z_leader == "Stegerwald" or z_leader == "Adenauer") and dnvp_ideology == "Radical" and not kvp_cnblp_sister and not dkp_merger_waiting
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
tags: event
face-image: img/e56pb91f26ag1.png


 The <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span> is a pan-socialist party, there is no denying that. The scope of this pan-socialism can be debated, however.

Following the <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**LU**</span>'s disasterous loss in Parliament, the party returned to its revolutionary roots, renaming to the <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**Revolutionary Socialist Worker's Party**</span> while losing its Market Socialist elmenats along the way.

The next test for the <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span> lies in the new <span style="color: #700000;">**Communist Party**</span>, with their former leader defecting to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span>.

Seeking to rally the non-<span style="color: #700000;">**Communist**</span> left, talks between the <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span> and the smaller Eco-Socialist and Anarchist <span style="color: #00963B;">**GAY**</span>. Eventually, the negotiations bare fruit and a proposal to merge <span style="color: #00963B;">**GAY**</span> into the  <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span> is tabled.

Now, at the party conference, the matter shall be settled, perhaps for good.


- @cvp_kvp_merger: The <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span> absorbs <span style="color: #00963B;">**GAY**</span>!
- @status_quo: The <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span>, quite unexpectedly, refuses to merge with <span style="color: #00963B;">**GAY**</span>!

@cvp_kvp_merger
subtitle: The <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span> desires the boost the merger with <span style="color: #00963B;">**GAY**</span> will provide.
unavailable-subtitle: The merger was suprisingly unpopular, with <span style="color: #00963B;">**GAY**</span> being viewed as too <span style="color: #FFB6C1;">**reformist**</span> for the <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span>
choose-if: z_relation < 40 and not ((in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or (spd_prussia and not in_left_front_prussia and not in_spd_majority_prussia)))
on-arrival: z_party_name = "CVP"; workers_z -= 3; workers_spd += 3; unemployed_z -= 3; unemployed_spd += 3
face-image: img/cvp.jpg
go-to: cvp_kvp_formed if kvp_formed; cvp_kvp_lite_formed if not kvp_formed

The [? if z_leader == "Stegerwald": <span style="color: #000000;">Center Party</span>?][? if z_leader == "Adenauer": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] has officially absorbed the much smaller <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, expanding its reach to the right. Unsurprisingly, this has severely strained relations between our two parties, as former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> figures like Westarp remain openly hostile to any cooperation with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>.

Still, the party’s transformation marches on. [? if z_leader == "Stegerwald": To mark the merger—and its progress toward becoming an interconfessional Volkspartei—it has formally rebranded itself as the <i>Christliche Volkspartei</i> (<span style="color: #000000;">Christian People's Party</span>)—an effort to finally shed its old, Catholic-associated <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span> label. ?]

@status_quo
subtitle: <span style="color: #00963B;">**GAY**</span>'s perceived focus on electoralism manages to give the opposition a convincing scapegoat.
choose-if: z_relation >= 40 or (in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition or in_popular_front or (spd_prussia and not in_left_front_prussia and not in_spd_majority_prussia))
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #A60A3D;">**RSWP**</span> is dead-set on the merger.
on-arrival: z_relation += 10; z_party_name = "CVP"; pro_republic += 5; nationalism -= 3; rural_kvp -= 2; rural_other -= 2 if not kvp_formed; rural_z += 2
face-image: img/zentrum_2.jpg

The status quo prevails. The [? if z_leader == "Stegerwald": <span style="color: #000000;">Center Party</span>?][? if z_leader == "Adenauer": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] and the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> will remain separate—at least for now. Perhaps this is proof enough that the party still values cooperation with us over chasing after every fragment of the old Right.

Even so, the party’s transformation presses on. [? if z_leader == "Stegerwald": To cement its evolution into an interconfessional *Volkspartei*, it has formally rebranded itself as the <i>Christliche Volkspartei</i> (<span style="color: #000000;">Christian People's Party</span>)—a move to finally shed its old, Catholic-associated <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span> label. ?]

